#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3812
#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3826
msgid "Large Uploads Mode"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3817
msgid "This mode improves backup performance for extensive media libraries. You can try to enable it if backups are slow or fail because of a large number of files in the uploads folder. This mode only supports ZipArchive, it will not work with PclZip"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3836
msgid "WPDB option has a better compatibility, but the speed of backup and restore is slower."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3847
msgid "It is recommended to choose PDO option if pdo_mysql extension is installed on your server, which lets you backup and restore your site faster."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3858
msgid "Backup compression method"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3863
msgid "ZipArchive"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3868
msgid "ZipArchive has a better flexibility which provides a higher backup success rate and speed. It is also the default zip method WPvivid pro uses. Using this method requires the ZIP extension to be installed within your PHP."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3873
msgid "PclZip"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3879
msgid "PclZip is a much slower but more stable zip method that is included in every WordPress install. WPvivid will automatically switch to PclZip if the ZIP extension is not installed within your PHP."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3890
msgid "Backup performance mode"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3895
msgid "Low (Balanced)"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3900
msgid "Low (Balanced): Use this default setting for minimal server resource usage, but expect longer backup times. Best for shared hosting or limited resources. Backups are split into 200MB chunks."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3906
msgid "Mid (Standard)"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3911
msgid "Mid (Standard): This mode offers a good balance between backup speed and resource usage. It's suitable for most web hosting environments."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3917
msgid "High (Accelerated)"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3922
msgid "High (Accelerated): This mode uses more server resources to reduce backup time, but is only recommended for dedicated servers. If backups time out or get stuck, consider Mid or Low mode. Backups are split into 4GB chunks."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3928
msgid "Custom (Advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3933
msgid "Custom (Advanced): This mode allows fine-tuning of backup parameters. Incorrect configuration can lead to backup failures. It is recommended to use only with specific guidance from our support team."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3943
msgid "The number of files compressed to the backup zip each time"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3947
msgid "When taking a backup, the plugin will compress this number of files to the backup zip each time. The default value is 500. The lower the value, the longer time the backup will take, but the higher the backup success rate. If you encounter a backup timeout issue, try to decrease this value."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3954
msgid "split a backup every this size"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3958
msgid "Some web hosting providers limit large zip files (e.g. 200MB), and therefore splitting your backup into many parts is an ideal way to avoid hitting the limitation if you are running a big website. Please try to adjust the value if you are encountering backup errors. When you set a value of 0MB, backups will be split every 4GB."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3965
msgid "The number of database tables compressed to each zip"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3969
msgid "When taking a database backup, the plugin will compress this number of tables to each backup zip. The default value is 1000 which works for most websites."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3976
msgid "split a sql file every this size"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3980
msgid "Some web hosting providers limit large files, therefore, splitting your sql files into many parts is an ideal way to avoid hitting the limitation. Please try to adjust the value if you get a backup timeout error. The default value is 400, and it is not recommended to set the value lower than 100."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3987
msgid "exclude files larger than this size"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3991
msgid "Using the option will ignore the file larger than the certain size in MB when backing up, '0' (zero) means unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:3998
msgid "maximum PHP script execution time for a backup task"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4002
msgid "The time-out is not your server PHP time-out. With the execution time exhausted, our plugin will shut the process of backup down. If the progress of backup encounters a time-out, that means you have a medium or large sized website, please try to scale the value bigger."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4009
msgid "maximum PHP memory for a backup task"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4013
msgid "Adjust this value to apply for a temporary PHP memory limit for WPvivid backup plugin to run a backup. We set this value to 256M by default. Increase the value if you encounter a memory exhausted error. Note: some web hosting providers may not support this."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4020
msgid "chunk size"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4024
msgid "e.g. if you choose a chunk size of 2MB, a 8MB file will use 4 chunks. Decreasing this value will break the ISP's transmission limit, for example:512KB"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4476
msgid "DB Copy Count"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4482
msgid "Number of DB rows, that are copied within one ajax query. The higher value makes the database copy process faster. Please try a high value to find out the highest possible value. If you encounter timeout errors, try lower values until no more errors occur."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4485
msgid "DB Replace Count"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4491
msgid "Number of DB rows, that are processed within one ajax query. The higher value makes the DB replacement process faster. If timeout erros occur, decrease the value because this process consumes a lot of memory."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4494
msgid "File Copy Count"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4500
msgid "Number of files to copy that will be copied within one ajax request. The higher value makes the file file copy process faster. Please try a high value to find out the highest possible value. If you encounter timeout errors, try lower values until no more errors occur."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4503
msgid "Max File Size"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4509
msgid "Maximum size of the files copied to a staging site. All files larger than this value will be ignored. If you set the value of 0 MB, all files will be copied to a staging site."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4512
msgid "Staging Memory Limit"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4518
msgid "Adjust this value to apply for a temporary PHP memory limit for %s while creating a staging site. We set this value to 256M by default. Increase the value if you encounter a memory exhausted error. Note: some web hosting providers may not support this."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4521
msgid "PHP Script Execution Timeout"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4527
msgid "The time-out is not your server PHP time-out. With the execution time exhausted, our plugin will shut down the progress of creating a staging site. If the progress  encounters a time-out, that means you have a medium or large sized website. Please try to scale the value bigger."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4530
msgid "Delay Between Requests"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4536
msgid "A lower value will help speed up the process of creating a staging site. However, if your server has a limit on the number of requests, a higher value is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4540
msgid "Retrying"
msgstr ""

#: addons2/backup_pro/class-wpvivid-setting-addon.php:4556
